Subject: [PATCH] Build incremental backup names from basenames and check copies

When editing an incremental backup, derive the next backup name from its basename rather than joining an absolute filename to its directory again. Abort both incremental-backup paths if the previous bytes cannot be copied, before overwriting the current file. The behavior is shared by desktop and Wasm.

Related upstream issue: https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=421792
That report fixed filename-only matching for incremental paths; its official issue and comments were inspected. The opened-backup branch still used a full path and ignored copy failures in the pinned revision. Searches found no separate report for these remaining failures.

diff --git a/libs/ui/KisViewManager.cpp b/libs/ui/KisViewManager.cpp
--- a/libs/ui/KisViewManager.cpp
+++ b/libs/ui/KisViewManager.cpp
@@ -1107,7 +1107,7 @@
         int intVersion = version.toInt(0);
         ++intVersion;
         QString baseNewVersion = QString::number(intVersion);
-        QString backupFileName = document()->localFilePath();
+        QString backupFileName = fileName;
         while (baseNewVersion.length() < version.length()) {
             baseNewVersion.prepend("0");
         }
@@ -1135,7 +1135,12 @@
             QMessageBox::critical(mainWindow(), i18nc("@title:window", "Couldn't save incremental backup"), i18n("Alternative names exhausted, try manually saving with a higher number"));
             return;
         }
-        QFile::copy(path + '/' + fileName, path + '/' + backupFileName);
+        if (!QFile::copy(path + '/' + fileName, path + '/' + backupFileName)) {
+            QMessageBox::critical(mainWindow(),
+                                  i18nc("@title:window", "Couldn't save incremental backup"),
+                                  i18n("Could not save %1.", path + '/' + backupFileName));
+            return;
+        }
         document()->saveAs(path + '/' + fileName, document()->mimeType(), true);
     }
     else { // if NOT working on a backup...
@@ -1169,8 +1174,13 @@
         } while (fileAlreadyExists);
 
         // Save both as backup and on current file for interapplication workflow
+        if (!QFile::copy(path + '/' + fileName, path + '/' + backupFileName)) {
+            QMessageBox::critical(mainWindow(),
+                                  i18nc("@title:window", "Couldn't save incremental backup"),
+                                  i18n("Could not save %1.", path + '/' + backupFileName));
+            return;
+        }
         document()->setFileBatchMode(true);
-        QFile::copy(path + '/' + fileName, path + '/' + backupFileName);
         document()->saveAs(path + '/' + fileName, document()->mimeType(), true);
         document()->setFileBatchMode(false);
     }
